    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T08:03:54Z",
    "body": "**Licence change upstream - nothing is borrowed from SolidCraft (2026-11-12).** Found while estimating #655: SolidCraft commit 312454f899 (2026-11-10, its PR 14578) added `LICENSE-BRAND`, the \"SolidCraft Brand and Interface Licence\", covering `crates/ui-kit`, `crates/look` (the interface icon masters, now under `crates/look/icons/design/svg`, glyphs and built-in themes) and `crates/theme`. Using any of it in another program needs the SolidCraft maintainers' written permission first. The earlier comment here (\"MIT OR Apache-2.0 ... about 30 icons can be borrowed\") is out of date for the current tree.\n\nSo the worker on slice 1 has been told: copy nothing from SolidCraft, draw originals or use Tabler (MIT) only, follow Tabler's conventions so the new icons sit with the ones we ship, and report and remove anything already taken. Whether CamCraft adopts SolidCraft's look at all is now a question for the maintainer and upstream (see the estimates on #655, #658, #659).",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
